---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "2 May 2026";
---

<Layout title={`intrebit — Privacy`}>
    <div class="legal">
        <header class="legal__header" transition:name="legal-header">
            <h1 transition:name="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="legal__meta" transition:name="legal-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        </header>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <p>
                We keep things simple. We don’t sell data, we don’t run creepy trackers, and we only collect
                what we need to run this website.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>What we collect</h2>
            <p>
                When you visit <strong>intrebit.com</strong>, we process a small amount of technical data to
                keep the site secure, prevent abuse, and understand basic usage.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Server/security logs (Cloudflare + our servers):</strong> IP address, request metadata, and security signals</li>
                <li><strong>Basic device + browser info:</strong> device type, browser, and screen size (coarse)</li>
                <li><strong>Page-level usage:</strong> pages visited and referrer domain (where you came from)</li>
                <li><strong>Approximate location:</strong> country-level location derived from IP address</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We do not use this information to identify you personally, and we don’t sell it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>What we don’t do</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>No advertising trackers</li>
                <li>No selling or renting personal data</li>
                <li>No user profiles</li>
                <li>No “follow you around the internet” stuff</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>Cookies</h2>
            <p>
                We do not use advertising or marketing cookies. Our website may use <strong>strictly necessary</strong>
                cookies for security and basic functionality (for example, Cloudflare protection features).
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>Analytics</h2>
            <p>
                We use <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> — a privacy-friendly, EU-hosted analytics service —
                to understand how the website is used and to improve it. Plausible records aggregate metrics
                only: <strong>page views</strong>, referrer domain, country, and coarse device/browser info
                (device type, browser, screen size).
            </p>
            <p>
                Plausible <strong>does not use cookies</strong>, does not collect personal data, and does not
                track visitors across sites. No advertising IDs, no fingerprinting, no cross-site tracking, no
                user profiles.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Identifiers:</strong> we do not store persistent identifiers such as long-lived visitor IDs.
                Plausible derives a daily, hashed signal from IP + user-agent solely to count unique visits per day,
                and discards it after 24 hours.
            </p>
            <p>
                More information is available in the{" "}
                <a class="legal__link" href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    Plausible data policy
                </a>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>Legal bases (EEA/UK)</h2>
            <p>
                Where GDPR applies, we process:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Site security and reliability data</strong> on the basis of <strong>legitimate interests</strong>.</li>
                <li><strong>Contact messages</strong> to take steps at your request / to respond (<strong>performance of a contract</strong> or <strong>legitimate interests</strong> depending on context).</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>Retention</h2>
            <p>
                We keep data only for as long as needed:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> stored in aggregate where possible; raw event data is kept for a limited period and then deleted or aggregated.</li>
                <li><strong>Security logs:</strong> retained for a limited period for security and troubleshooting.</li>
                <li><strong>Contact messages:</strong> retained only as long as needed to respond and for reasonable follow-up.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>Sharing and processors</h2>
            <p>
                We use a small number of service providers to run the site. They process data on our behalf
                under appropriate safeguards:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — CDN, hosting, and security/abuse protection.</li>
                <li><strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> — privacy-friendly, EU-hosted website analytics.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We do not sell or share personal data with advertisers.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>Your rights</h2>
            <p>
                Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or object to our processing.
                To make a request, email us.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <p>
                If you contact us (by email or contact form), we process the information you provide (such as your
                email address, name, and message) so we can respond.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>We use your message only to reply and handle your request.</li>
                <li>We do not add you to marketing lists unless you explicitly ask.</li>
                <li>We keep contact messages only as long as needed to respond and for a short period afterward for follow-up.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                <a class="legal__link" href="/contact" data-email-user="hello" data-email-host="intrebit.com">Email us</a>
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</Layout>